From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] qt: let the frontend ask for VK_KHR_display direct output

The Vulkan renderer already implements WindowInfo::Type::VulkanDirect
end to end. Nothing in the Qt frontend ever produced that type, so the
path was unreachable. Add the one branch that does.

--- a/pcsx2-qt/QtUtils.h
+++ b/pcsx2-qt/QtUtils.h
@@ -128,6 +128,32 @@
 		QPlatformNativeInterface* pni = QGuiApplication::platformNativeInterface();
 		const QString platform_name = QGuiApplication::platformName();
 
+		// Direct-to-display through VK_KHR_display, for a handheld that boots
+		// straight into a game and is configured from files rather than from a
+		// settings UI. The renderer already implements this end to end -
+		// instance extension selection in GSDeviceVK::SelectInstanceExtensions(),
+		// surface creation through vkCreateDisplayPlaneSurfaceKHR() in
+		// VKSwapChain::CreateSurface() - but nothing in the frontend ever
+		// produced the window type that reaches it, so the whole path was
+		// unreachable.
+		//
+		// No native handle is supplied and none is needed: the renderer
+		// enumerates displays itself. Passing 0x0 asks it for the display's
+		// preferred mode, and it writes the real width, height and refresh rate
+		// back into this structure. Returning here rather than falling through
+		// to the Qt geometry and refresh-rate queries below is deliberate - the
+		// QPA platform is offscreen in this mode, so those would describe a
+		// window that is not on the panel.
+		if (qEnvironmentVariableIntValue("ARMSX2_VULKAN_DIRECT") != 0)
+		{
+			wi.type = WindowInfo::Type::VulkanDirect;
+			wi.surface_width = 0;
+			wi.surface_height = 0;
+			wi.surface_scale = 1.0f;
+			INFO_LOG("Using VK_KHR_display direct-to-monitor; no compositor.");
+			return wi;
+		}
+
 		QWindow* windowHandle;
 		if constexpr (std::is_base_of_v<QWidget, T>)
 			windowHandle = window->windowHandle();
